17] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458875 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186458944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186458903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459202 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fe68fa49-351f-5bc9-8911-9305bb6e6c31" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1069 "q-281027" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(3,1,2),$ $B(0,5,0),$ $C(3,3,1),$ and $D(1,4,2).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a41586e-8435-5507-a7ef-851c0478678b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459212 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(5j)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+4j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,4,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+3j+1k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-1k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(1i+4j+2k)-(3i+1j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+3j \\\\  & =⟨-2,3,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|-4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(2\\cdot 0-(-1)(3))-4(0\\cdot 0-(-1)(-2))+(-2)(0\\cdot 3-2\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =-3(3)-4(-2)-2(4) \\\\  & =-9-8+8 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459142 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280323" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(1,1,1),$ $B(2,3,4),$ $C(-1,2,0),$ and $D(3,0,5).$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "250fb4d2-3fa7-5b45-a7da-bbdf1bb4b98b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459217 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-i+2j)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(3i+5k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i-j+4k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot (-1))-2((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3((-2)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1(4-1)-2(-8+2)+3(2-2) \\\\  & =3+12+0 \\\\  & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|15|=15.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $k$ given that the vectors $p=⟨5,-2,2⟩,$ $q=⟨3,k,1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-8,3,-4⟩$ are coplanar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2eedb023-f05d-5365-a7fb-580375aea9cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459221 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & k & 1 \\\\ -8 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ -8 & -4\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ -8 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5(k\\cdot (-4)-3\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot (-4)-(-8)\\cdot 1)+2(3\\cdot 3-(-8)\\cdot k) \\\\  & =-20k-15-8+18+16k \\\\  & =-4k-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ -4k-5 & =0 \\\\ k & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=-\\frac{5}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128486" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(8,0,5),$ $B(8,-3,3),$ $C(5,2,5),$ and $D(7,-1,4).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5208cfc4-b7ed-5787-b174-631ca841e3f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459239 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(8i-3j+3k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(5i+2j+5k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-3i+2j \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(7i-j+4k)-(8i+5k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+3((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =9-10 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-1|=1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42055" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-1,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨1,-4,2⟩$ and $c=⟨0,5,1⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8fcc06ee-9e96-5a19-8006-dabebc81e1fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459261 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-((-4)\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 2)-2(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2)+5(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =14-2+25 \\\\  & =37\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|37|=37.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459098 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128457" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $t$ given that the vectors $p=⟨9,9,-2⟩,$ $q=⟨5,6,0⟩,$ and $r=⟨4,t,t⟩$ are coplanar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1fc629c-e7ef-51c7-b925-1dba79c32351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459264 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 9 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 4 & t & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ t & t\\end{aligned}|-9\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & t\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 6 \\\\ 4 & t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9(6\\cdot t-t\\cdot 0)-9(5\\cdot t-4\\cdot 0)-2(5\\cdot t-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =54t-45t-10t+48 \\\\  & =48-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =0 \\\\ 48-t & =0 \\\\ t & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $t=48.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42053" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,2,4⟩$, $b=⟨3,5,-7⟩$ and $c=⟨1,0,2⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b387009d-e229-5370-99a6-bec87fcc7e69" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459275 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & -7 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-7))-2(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot (-7))+4(3\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =10-26-20 \\\\  & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|-36|=36.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1069 "q-128471" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD},$ given the points $A(0,9,4),$ $B(3,8,2),$ $C(2,9,1),$ and $D(-1,7,7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bf74fac3-a1be-5590-922d-8474c31e9763" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459280 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+8j+2k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i-j-2k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+9j+k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =2i-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(-i+7j+7k)-(9j+4k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(0\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-3))+(2\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot (-3))-2(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =-18+3+8 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-7|=7.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459172 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280710" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨4,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨1,3,0⟩$, and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c8774189-53cd-55b6-bea0-346937f16124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459283 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)+0+2(1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 0) \\\\  & =60+0+4 \\\\  & =64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|64|=64.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459199 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1069 "q-20144" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$, given the points $A(3,-2,2)$, $B(4,3,2)$, $C(1,3,5)$, $D(2,4,-6).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da5d7cb9-5c27-5b41-96e4-8767d3252a54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459292 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the displacement vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ that span the parallelepiped:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+3j+2k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =i+5j \\\\  & =⟨1,5,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+3j+5k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i+5j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,5,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AD} & =d-a \\\\  & =(2i+4j-6k)-(3i-2j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+6j-8k \\\\  & =⟨-1,6,-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the volume of the parallelepiped, we need to take the absolute value of the triple product of the above vectors.\n\nComputing the triple product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\cdot (\\overset{\\to }{AC}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AD}) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 6 & -8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -8\\end{aligned}|-5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -8\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(5\\cdot (-8)-6\\cdot 3)-5((-2)\\cdot (-8)-(-1)\\cdot 3)+0 \\\\  & =-58-95 \\\\  & =-153.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of the corresponding parallelpiped spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB},$ $\\overset{\\to }{AC},$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AD}$ is\n\n$$\nV=|-153|=153.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1069 "q-18262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, $q=⟨-2,3,1⟩$ and $r=⟨-1,4,3⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f94fb95c-1aca-535d-ab25-0d9749d43fb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459306 #edb/ref 1074 "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0-((-2)\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 1)-((-2)\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =5+5 \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|10|=10.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186459137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1069 "q-18261" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $x$ given that the vectors $a=⟨12,-2x,1⟩$ , $b=⟨1,5,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨-9,4,8⟩$  are coplanar." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa437fb9-bfe8-5dbc-864c-e499156b0343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186459308 #edb/ref 1074 "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}12 & -2x & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 4 & 8\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{aligned}|-(-2x)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 8\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12(5\\cdot 8-4\\cdot (-2))+2x(1\\cdot 8-(-9)\\cdot (-2))+(1\\cdot 4-5\\cdot (-9)) \\\\  & =576-20x+49 \\\\  & =625-20x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =0 \\\\ 625-20x & =0 \\\\ 20x & =625 \\\\ x & =\\frac{125}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $x=\\frac{125}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
